Sval: Remove Firefox's selectable profiles

Selectable profiles let one install hold a group of profiles, switched
from the File menu, the app menu and a selector window at startup. Sval
keeps its data in one directory (one-data-directory.patch) and locked
the feature off, so it goes whole: the component and its pages, menus,
Settings sections, startup hook, actor, prompts, strings, prefs, the
Firefox account sign-in warnings that offered another profile, the
migrator that refreshed a profile in a group, the window title's
profile name and the messaging targeting attributes. The profile
manager's windows go with them: about:profiles, the -P profile
selection dialog and its new profile wizard. In Gecko the
MOZ_SELECTABLE_PROFILES define goes, and with it the profile service's
selector flag, the selector launched at startup, its observer and the
reset path for a profile in a group. A profile's store ID is read-only;
the profile group datastore that holds Nimbus's enrollments, and the
toolkit.profiles.storeID pref it reads, stay. The component's metrics
file also defined profile.lock.failed_lock_count, which Telemetry
records at startup, so that metric moves to toolkit/profile's.

